msgid "We use PostHog’s EU service to understand how Lymi is used. On the public site we count visits without cookies or any identifier stored on your device: PostHog derives a visitor code from the day, your IP address and browser, then discards the address, so a visit cannot be linked to another day’s. In the app, we link product activity to your opaque account identifier. We send page categories, published deck slugs, fixed action labels, counts, review grades, app language, the referring website, limited campaign details and the country of the visit, which our hosting provider determines. When you sign up, your account records where your visit began. We do not send card content, email addresses, names, credentials or private requested URLs, and we do not record sessions. We do this on the basis of our legitimate interest in understanding and improving Lymi. To object, email <0>hello@lymi.app</0> and we will stop product analytics for your account."
msgstr "We use PostHog’s EU service to understand how Lymi is used. On the public site we count visits without cookies or any identifier stored on your device: PostHog derives a visitor code from the day, your IP address and browser, then discards the address, so a visit cannot be linked to another day’s. In the app, we link product activity to your opaque account identifier. We send page categories, published deck slugs, fixed action labels, counts, review grades, app language, the referring website, limited campaign details and the country of the visit, which our hosting provider determines. When you sign up, your account records where your visit began. We do not send card content, email addresses, names, credentials or private requested URLs, and we do not record sessions. We do this on the basis of our legitimate interest in understanding and improving Lymi. To object, email <0>hello@lymi.app</0> and we will stop product analytics for your account."

